fixture-ssh-key / fixture-ssh-key.pub — VM TEST FIXTURE, checked in on purpose.

An ed25519 keypair that authorises `mura` on the on-demand VM tests only (tests/vm/lib.nix
declares the public half via the standard `users.users.mura.openssh.authorizedKeys.keys`).
It proves the self-builder path of first-run-onboarding.md §5.3: on an image you built
yourself, SSH works from first boot with a declared key even though the account has no
password. Like the fixture password hash in fixture-user.nix, it is never in a shipped image.

Secret scanners will flag the private half. That is expected — treat it as public. Rotating it
is `ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -N "" -f tests/vm/fixture-ssh-key` (OpenSSH rejects comment lines
inside the private key file, which is why this note is a sibling file).
